32. RESPONSIVE AND DEVICE BEHAVIOR

The interface must work on realistic mobile dimensions.

Do not design only for one giant modern phone.

Account for:

- small screens
- large screens
- safe areas
- status bars
- keyboard
- dynamic text
- scrolling
- orientation where applicable

Touch targets should be comfortably usable.

Minimum target should generally be around 44–48 points.

---

33. ACCESSIBILITY

Support:

- readable contrast
- screen-reader labels
- meaningful accessibility names
- dynamic text where practical
- reduced motion
- sufficient touch targets
- clear focus/selection states

Icons must communicate their purpose.

Spoiler controls must be understandable without relying only on color.

The PDF's accessibility requirements include WCAG AA contrast, minimum 44×44pt touch targets, screen-reader labels and reduced-motion support. These principles remain useful here.

