The build is not complete until:

PRODUCT

- Hallyu branding is preserved.
- The current multi-world entertainment direction is represented.
- The product feels like one unified ecosystem.

FRONTEND

- The application runs locally.
- Screens are implemented as real frontend code.
- Navigation works.
- Interactions work.
- Forms work.
- Scrolling works.
- Sheets/modals work.
- States work.

UX

- The primary user journeys work from beginning to end.
- No major dead ends exist.
- Loading, empty, error, offline and guest states are handled.

VISUAL

- The interface is cinematic and premium.
- Typography is readable.
- Hierarchy is strong.
- Spacing is consistent.
- Motion is purposeful.
- Entertainment content remains visually dominant.

TECHNICAL

- Existing project architecture is respected.
- Reusable components are used.
- No unnecessary architectural rewrite.
- No unresolved runtime errors.
- No obvious touch/hit-testing bugs.
- Local preview is stable.

MOST IMPORTANT

Open the app and use it like an actual person.

Do not merely inspect the source code.

Tap everything.

Scroll everything.

Open everything.

Close everything.

Navigate everywhere.

Submit things.

Go back.

Try edge cases.

If something does not work, fix it.

The final result should be a working Hallyu frontend product, not documentation describing what somebody else should eventually build.

